ction along separate parallel tracks. The LEFT far leg on SCREEN-LEFT is ahead along its own track (slightly UP-RIGHT); its foot rolls flat on ground taking weight. The RIGHT near leg on SCREEN-RIGHT trails slightly DOWN-LEFT along its own parallel track, heel rising while toe remains grounded.",
